{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789500378,"nonce":"nHFdgcxI3kHiuGMkyWBn+Dn4pm4=","message":"Electron/Pi viability spike committed as 3602cf5 on branch spike-electron-app-shell.\n\nPackaged macOS arm64 app passed direct launch without dev server or sidecar, sandbox/context-isolation boundary checks, opaque-ID document tests, deterministic Pi streaming over IPC, cancellation, renderer callback, and close lifecycle. The spike uses the maintained @earendil-works/pi-ai and pi-agent-core 0.85.1 successor packages in Electron main, not pi-coding-agent.\n\nRecorded tradeoff: unsigned app is 365 MB and multi-process, versus the Tauri spike at 8.5 MB with one executable. Native dialog interaction, real Codex/OpenCode authentication, and Windows packaging remain unproven. Recommendation: prefer Tauri for static authoring and retain Electron as the provider-compatibility fallback if a focused Tauri Pi/auth spike proves too fragile or requires an unacceptable sidecar.","files":null}]}